  "body": "Found while checking #2610 (closed: not a bug). The second reviewer found one case where the cancellation behind `G10 L20 P<n> X[#5420-#190]` (active offset + deviation, see #2610) is not exact: a work offset with an XY rotation. Then the probed deviation is in the rotated frame, and adding it to the target origin may move the target WCS by the wrong vector. This applies even when the target is the active WCS, so it is a different defect from #2610's title.\n\n**Unconfirmed:** read from the code and the algebra only; nothing was built or run. If a test confirms it, this is wrong posted output and becomes P1.\n\nWhat to check: whether the Tormach/LinuxCNC probe posts can be used with a rotated WCS at all (a refusal would also be a correct answer), and what LinuxCNC's G10 L20 does with the rotation word.\n\nDone means: either a test that shows the result is right with a rotated WCS, or a fix (or a refusal by name) pinned by a test.\n",
